Gideon for Debian/Ubuntu
========================

Ollama is a prerequisite
------------------------
Everything Gideon needs is bundled in this package except the language model
backend. Gideon talks to Ollama over HTTP at http://localhost:11434, and the
package deliberately does not vendor it: Ollama is a separate ~3GB upstream
product with its own release cadence and its own model store.

Without Ollama, Gideon still installs, starts, listens for the wake word and
transcribes speech - but answering fails with:

    could not connect to Ollama at http://localhost:11434 - is 'ollama serve' running?

To satisfy it:

    ollama serve &            # or run it however you normally do
    ollama pull qwen2.5:1.5b  # the model named in /etc/gideon/config.yaml

The tray icon's dashboard has an "LLM" toggle that starts and stops
`ollama serve` for you, provided the `ollama` binary is on PATH.

Known limitations
-----------------
* Stopping Ollama from the tray runs `pkill -f "ollama serve"`. That matches
  any process of yours whose command line contains that string, not only the
  one Gideon started. If you run other `ollama serve` processes, stop them
  yourself rather than using the toggle.

* The service is enabled with `systemctl --global enable`, which takes effect
  at each user's next login. A package install cannot reliably start a user
  service in an already-running session, so after installing run:

      systemctl --user start gideon.service

* The tray icon needs a StatusNotifierItem host. On stock Ubuntu GNOME that is
  the `gnome-shell-extension-appindicator` package (a Recommends, normally
  already present). Without it Gideon runs headless-but-working: the wake word
  and voice pipeline are fine, but the "Ask..." popup and dashboard are
  unreachable because there is no icon to click.

* This package targets Ubuntu 24.04 (noble) on amd64. The bundled runtime is
  self-contained, but the GTK and PyGObject packages it depends on differ on
  other releases. preinst warns rather than refusing, so installing elsewhere
  is possible but untested.

Configuration
-------------
/etc/gideon/config.yaml     model choices, audio devices, prompt
/etc/default/gideon         environment (offline guards, thread limits)

Both are dpkg conffiles, so your edits survive package upgrades.

Logs go to the journal:

    journalctl --user -u gideon.service -f
